    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d482">

                <pb facs="0402" n="394" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg394"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11545: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)<anchor n="32" xml:id="d482-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-09T17:00:00-05:00">December 9, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>335. Your 609, December 9, 5 p.m. While no objection is perceived to your
                    reminding the Foreign Office of the assurances repeatedly <pb facs="0403"
                        n="395" xml:id="pg395"/> given with regard to safeguarding lives and
                    property of non-combatants, the Department considers it inadvisable as no
                    Americans are known to have been injured for you to request that an
                    investigation be made or to urge that those responsible be severely dealt
                        with.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d482-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d482-f1" n="32" type="source" xml:id="d482-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated in telegram No. 391 for the information of the Embassy in China.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d482-f2" n="33" xml:id="d482-f2-content">
                <p>The Ambassador in Japan in telegram No. 610, December 10, 11 a.m., reported no
                    action was taken, but that “we will look for an early opportunity to remind the
                    Foreign Office of assurances given regarding safety of lives and property.”
                    (793.94/11555)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
